---
description: Required star is viewer chrome; shared viewer helpers are OK
globs: **/*.ts,**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

# Viewer owns the required star

Showing `*` for `params.required` is the **field viewer’s** job. List chrome,
draft rows, and orchestrators do not probe `required` or paint the mark.

If several field viewers share the same mark, **factor it as viewer chrome**
(`RequiredMark`). The viewer still composes it. Heading/panel viewers do not.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — draft/list chrome sniffs a field-only key
const required = "required" in item.params && item.params.required === true;

// ✅ GOOD — the field viewer shows the star
field: {
  viewer: ({ props: { formItem } }) => (
    <>
      {formItem.params.name}
      {formItem.params.required ? " *" : ""}
    </>
  ),
}

// ✅ ALSO GOOD — shared mark chrome, still composed by the field viewer
field: {
  viewer: ({ props: { formItem } }) => (
    <>
      <FieldLabel name={formItem.params.name} />
      <RequiredMark required={formItem.params.required} />
    </>
  ),
}
```

`wrapWithRequired` is the **editor** toggle, not the star. Unanswered follow-up
rows go through Design’s list viewers (`FormDialogsEditor` embedded) so each
field viewer can show its own star.

Related: `no-per-type-extension.mdc`, `unify-demo-chrome.mdc`.
